1
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:09,044
SHIT, IT'S DARK IN HERE,
CAN'T SEE A DAMN THING,

2
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,700
WHERE THE HELL IS THAT BASTARD ANYWAY?

3
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:23,117
IT'S THE MIDDLE OF THE DAY AND I STILL
HAVE TO FEEL MY WAY AROUND THIS HOVEL,

4
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,612
THIS BETTER BE WORTH IT.

5
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:29,860
Okay, if I remember correctly,
I'll find Dio over in that room.

6
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:40,057
Disgusting, this little lady
must be one of Dio's leftovers!

7
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:42,697
Damn bras just throw
themselves at the guy.

8
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,617
Like having their blood drank
is the latest bedroom craze.

9
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:47,957
The whole thing's nutty if you ask me?

10
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,980
Though girls do tend
to go for the bad boys.

11
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,140
But forget about that.

12
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,237
I've never seen so much gold in my life.

13
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:56,614
How'd he get all this?

14
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:01,091
It seems like this guy can have
and do just about anything.

15
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:09,970
Horse.

16
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,560
What is it?

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:22,830
It's...

18
00:01:22,913 --> 00:01:23,743
Master... Dio.

19
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:32,600
Son of a bitch. What is this?

20
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:36,331
Just looking at him is enough
to send chills down my spine.

21
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,117
Keep it together, whole horse.

22
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,612
Don't let him spook you.

23
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:44,117
He's nothing to lose your cool over.

24
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,024
Yeah, he's not even that
much stronger than you.

25
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,500
I'll ask you again.

26
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:52,540
Did you want something, whole horns?

27
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,780
Uh, well, yes, actually.

28
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:57,217
There's something I
thought you ought to know.

29
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,777
I received intel that two
of the nine great gods,

30
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:02,357
Mariah and Alessi, have
been put out of commission.

31
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:03,920
And your point is?

32
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:06,360
Well, there's more.

33
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,071
We've got trouble coming.

34
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:11,217
Turns out Joestar and his gang
will arrive in Cairo tomorrow,

35
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,712
and only three of the nine gods are left.

36
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:16,291
It seems you've misunderstood my question.

37
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:19,699
I want to know what you're
going to do, whole horse.

38
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,257
You seem to have been
caught rather off guard.

39
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:26,222
I simply wish to know when you're
going to kill them, whole horse.

40
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:29,257
While it's true you've
pledged your allegiance to me,

41
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:32,800
you have yet to adequately
prove yourself in battle.

42
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:37,620
In this day and age, any
simpleton can deliver information.

43
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:42,600
Twice you've failed me, and
here you are crawling back.

44
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,380
You couldn't know this,

45
00:02:57,540 --> 00:03:01,217
but my body once belonged to a man
by the name of Jonathan Joestar.

46
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:04,860
Jonathan was the grandfather
of Joseph Joestar.

47
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:07,017
Look closely.

48
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:10,924
Notice how the left finger heals
at a slower rate than the right.

49
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:14,380
The left side of this body is weak,

50
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:17,980
which proves that it doesn't
completely belong to me yet.

51
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,280
And that I am not yet immortal.

52
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:24,520
I am ill-equipped to fight a battle
with Joestar and his friends.

53
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:34,560
Now then, if there is nothing else, run
along and destroy my enemies on my behalf.

54
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:39,020
Failure will most assuredly
result in your untimely demise.

55
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:41,577
You're burking up the wrong tree, Haas.

56
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:45,601
As if threats are gonna make me
roll over and do whatever you want.

57
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,000
On your behalf, my ass?

58
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:49,720
I'm no fool.

59
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,937
I'm smart enough to throw
in with whoever's strongest.

60
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:55,297
Everything I've said has been lip service.

61
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:58,733
I'd never swear my loyalty to
you at the cost of my soul.

62
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,100
Rat bastard, you're not so tough, are you?

63
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,820
You're wide open.

64
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:08,337
Guess having another person's body
attached to your head has made you go soft.

65
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,600
This is perfect.

66
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:12,117
I don't have to fight
Joseph and the other three.

67
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:14,494
Not when I've got Dio in my crosshairs.

68
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:19,724
It'd be a hell of a lot easier to blow his
head to smithereens right here and now.

69
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,031
If I do, his treasures mine for the Taken.

70
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,808
This'll be a piece of cake.

71
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:29,997
He doesn't know Emperor's
aimed point blank at his skull.

72
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:32,717
I can finish him off and
he'll be none the wiser.

73
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:36,388
Just one pull of the trigger
and this nightmare will be over.

74
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,118
After all, Emperor was made
for close combat carnage.

75
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,180
I can do this.

76
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:42,240
I can do this.

77
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:44,000
Is there a problem?

78
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,717
You seem to be hesitating.

79
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,820
Eat lead, shitbag!

80
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:52,480
I'm about to splatter your brains
all over the floor, Mr. Dio!

81
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:56,153
Are you positive you want to
go through with shooting me?

82
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,360
He's gone!

83
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,350
Fascinating.

84
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:10,117
As you prepared to fire,
your breathing was relaxed.

85
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,040
You didn't even perspire.

86
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:13,617
You were composed.

87
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:16,080
Very impressive, whole horse.

88
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,517
This doesn't make a lick of sense.

89
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,440
I didn't even see him move.

90
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,877
There's no way in hell he
could have creeped up behind

91
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:37,136
me without breaking a single
one of those spider webs.

92
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,110
Fast or not,

93
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:41,837
he shouldn't have been able to sneak up
to my rear without me noticing something.

94
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:45,200
Was that the power of Dio's stand?

95
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:49,020
The power of the world,
ill-equipped? Yeah, right.

96
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:54,597
I finally understand, Master Dio.

97
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:58,217
I've got no choice but to pledge
my eternal loyalty to you.

98
00:05:58,300 --> 00:05:59,760
You've got me beat.

99
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:13,780
I'll wake you in the morning.

100
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,820
In the end of the day of the world,

101
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:29,220
I'm afraid of the devil!

102
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:31,297
I'm afraid of the devil?

103
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:32,660
I'm afraid of him.

104
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:39,900
I'm afraid of him, I'm afraid of him.

105
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:50,680
Let's get started!

106
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:01,610
Stop!

107
00:07:01,693 --> 00:07:02,600
Stop! Stop!

108
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,920
End of the world?

109
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,680
That's the life's death.

110
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,077
Ola Ola Ola!

111
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,137
Ola Ola Ola Ola!

112
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:22,480
Ola Ola Ola Ola!

113
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:26,760
Ola Ola!

114
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:44,200
We'll be arriving on schedule at
Cairo International Airport shortly.

115
00:07:58,780 --> 00:07:59,610
Whoops.

116
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,073
Snooze you lose, buddy.

117
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:05,474
I hate to break it to you, cowboy,
but it looks like this is our cab now.

118
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:07,940
No hard feelings.

119
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,430
Huh?

120
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:12,875
Don't tell me you're going
to start crying like a baby!

121
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,630
Shit!

122
00:08:18,713 --> 00:08:19,543
What the hell?

123
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:24,380
Giza Pronto.

124
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:25,954
The Mona House Hotel.

125
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:35,377
I'm going to open up this
suitcase and let you out.

126
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:38,717
Unless you want some grade A
pain, I suggest you keep calm.

127
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:39,740
We clear? Huh?

128
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:42,077
Did you, uh, say something just now, sir?

129
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:44,297
If I did, it sure the hell wasn't to you.

130
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:46,145
Now shut up and drive the cab.

131
00:08:46,660 --> 00:08:47,490
Yes, sir.

132
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:58,920
Cut it out.

133
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:01,237
You know, if you weren't
making such a damn racket,

134
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:04,997
I would have had to hogtie you and put
you on the plane like a piece of luggage.

135
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,820
Don't be a baby, Mondatta.

136
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:10,057
Your brother's got another month in
the hospital thanks to that bomb,

137
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:11,597
so you and I are partners.

138
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:15,197
Now make sure those big ears are listening,
cause here's what we're gonna do.

139
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:19,357
We're gonna use your book of premonitions
and my assassin gun to stamp out Jotaro,

140
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,499
Joseph, and the rest of those SOBs.

141
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:22,718
Got that, Mondatta?

142
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:25,317
I get that we haven't
known each other long?

143
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,497
But from what I've gathered,

144
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:29,917
you're afraid of just about anyone
that's not your brother Zenyatta.

145
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,037
But don't you think this is the
perfect chance to avenge the guy?

146
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:36,157
You don't want to be a
yellow-bellied coward forever, right?

147
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,122
That's no good.

148
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,892
I'm out of options, too.

149
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:40,961
We've got no choice but to fight.

150
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:43,632
Time for us to get our revenge, Mondatta.

151
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,897
I'm gonna let you loose now,

152
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:49,597
but you have to swear to me you won't
carry on with all that infernal hollering,

153
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:50,510
okay?

154
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:52,940
See that, son?

155
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,380
I'm not so bad.

156
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,317
Now try and settle down, huh?

157
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:58,518
I don't need you getting sick on me.

158
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:01,717
Because believe it or not, I'm
on your side in this whole mess.

159
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:02,920
So don't you worry.

160
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,420
Just relax for now.

161
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:09,470
Huh?

162
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:15,500
Sir, why do you have
a puking kid? Shut up!

163
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:17,480
I see.

164
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,682
You got Moshe's sickness
from being on the plane.

165
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:24,360
Mondatta, let's be pals from here on.

166
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,560
How's that sound?

167
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:30,520
I'm Mondatta.

168
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,000
This is Holhorse.

169
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,400
He's mean, and I don't like him.

170
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:38,757
While Mondatta was sleeping, whole horse
tied him up and stuffed him in a trunk.

171
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:41,117
Mondatta was taken from
his brother, Zenyatta.

172
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:42,140
He was sad.

173
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:45,057
But even though Mondatta
was scared out of his mind,

174
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:46,797
he wanted to avenge his brother.

175
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:49,292
So he decided to work up his whole horse.

176
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:53,660
Oh, come on.

177
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:55,097
You won't even get near me?

178
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:59,077
Well, I guess you're trying, which
is all I can ask for at this point.

179
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,837
And by the way, i gotta know,

180
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:05,037
Does your stand really predict the future
or is that just some cockamamie rumor?

181
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:07,317
if that was all just a tall tale?

182
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,237
Then I brought you here for nothing.

183
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,197
I mean even with it.

184
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:12,456
Your brother got blown to high heaven

185
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:15,480
Which is it kid are you a fraud?

186
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:22,406
How did a new comic appear on a
blank page from out of nowhere?

187
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:25,157
Well mondatta and whole horse
were walking through the outskirts

188
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:28,817
of cairo They met a lady who was
as pretty as the day was long?

189
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:32,520
Then Whole Horse jump-kicked
the lady in the neck! Hmm?

190
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:35,517
The pretty lady was so
overjoyed about the kick

191
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:38,137
that out of the blue she
gave Whole Horse her jewels!

192
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,660
Yahoo! We're rich!

193
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,007
What the hell is this crap?!

194
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,276
You must think I was born last night!

195
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:48,097
You call this a prediction, Mondatta?

196
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:49,356
There's just no way!

197
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:51,737
This crap has to be made up or something!

198
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:53,180
I'm telling the truth.

199
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:54,640
I stand, boss.

200
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:56,977
You just have to trust in its prophecies.

201
00:11:57,060 --> 00:12:02,857
They're, they're, they're 100,
they're 100 % right every time.

202
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:04,340
They're right 100 %?

203
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,637
You trying to pull a wool over my eyes?

204
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,477
There's no way some
lady's going to give me

205
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:10,837
her jewels after jump
kicking her in the neck.

206
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:14,391
You'd have to be off your rocker
to do something like that.

207
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:23,340
Listen, Mondatta,

208
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:26,977
I'm proud to say that I'm a gentleman
and a proper gentleman at that.

209
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:29,397
Cause of that, I got
girls all over the world.

210
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:33,097
I might tell a white lie now and again,
but I'd never haul off and hit one.

211
00:12:33,180 --> 00:12:37,827
I respect all the ladies, the beauties,
the plain ones, and even the ugly ones.

212
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:42,337
There's no way your prediction
will ever come to pass.

213
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:45,737
Come hell or high water, I
swear I will never hit a woman.

214
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:48,457
She could pay me every dime,
nickel, and quarter she had.

215
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:50,257
I still wouldn't put my hands on her.

216
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:52,360
It's 100 % true, yes.

217
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:01,360
See there?

218
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:03,417
Your fancy prediction was wrong.

219
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:04,330
Huh?

220
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,780
Who the hell are you?!

221
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:30,210
What in the?

222
00:13:30,293 --> 00:13:32,219
There was a scorpion in your shawl!

223
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:35,174
This thing's sting is a death sentence!

224
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:36,090
What?

225
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:41,737
You spotted that wretched creature before
it had a chance to crawl into my clothes!

226
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:45,349
If you hadn't killed it, she
would have been stung for sure!

227
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:48,120
You saved my life!

228
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:50,100
Oh, please, let me repay you!

229
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:52,617
Would my necklace be a sufficient reward?

230
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:53,530
It's yours!

231
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:58,317
Boy, this is my lucky day.

232
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:00,517
Mountain and I are practically invincible.

233
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:02,397
We'll be the unstoppable duo.

234
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:09,480
I

235
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:12,830
don't

236
00:14:12,913 --> 00:14:13,743
think

237
00:14:13,826 --> 00:14:14,656
I'm gonna

238
00:14:14,739 --> 00:14:15,569
be able to help you folks.

239
00:14:15,652 --> 00:14:19,537
It's been my job to repair rooftops in
Cairo for around 40 years now and I can't

240
00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:23,557
say that I've ever seen a place like this
from the looks of the building's design.

241
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:27,057
The thing was built over a
hundred years ago, give or take.

242
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:29,777
If I had to take a guess,
based on the picture,

243
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:32,217
I'd say you'd find it
somewhere south of here.

244
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:36,535
The buildings in Cairo get older and
older the farther south you travel.

245
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:37,710
Huh?

246
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:39,828
I'm sorry I don't have
more to go on, Sonny.

247
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:41,540
No, don't worry about it.

248
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:42,681
Sorry to bother.

249
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,350
Hmm.

250
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:45,770
Hmm.

251
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:48,130
Hmm.

252
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:50,480
All right. Understood.

253
00:14:50,820 --> 00:14:52,114
Thanks for the update.

254
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:59,869
I decided to make a call to Japan, and
my daughter's condition is much worse.

255
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:02,512
She's lost virtually all of her strength.

256
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:05,052
At best, she has three or four days left.

257
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:12,980
I can almost feel it.

258
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,339
It's like Dio's right on top of us.

259
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:18,457
I'd bet anything that he's
hiding somewhere close by.

260
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:19,920
But where could he be?

261
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:21,560
And how do we find him?

262
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:23,397
We should get moving.

263
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:26,186
We'll talk to everyone
here until we find him.

264
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:27,410
Hmm.

265
00:15:27,493 --> 00:15:28,323
We've come this far.

266
00:15:28,406 --> 00:15:29,700
We have to keep going.

267
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:40,740
Been a long time coming, but
it's time for our grand reunion.

268
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:42,537
I'm getting sick of those faces.

269
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:45,097
I never thought they'd get so
close to Master Dio's mansion,

270
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:47,677
but they're on a collision
course for his backyard.

271
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:49,840
And by the way, listen, Mondatta!

272
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:59,077
We need to chat about
your latest prediction.

273
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:01,000
You sure it's 100 % foolproof?

274
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,465
It's more than a little wacky.

275
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:06,032
They're not dumb enough to fall for this.

276
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:11,680
My premonitions are always 100 % accurate.

277
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:13,317
Is that what you were going to say?

278
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:16,080
Well, they are, yes. Come on.

279
00:16:16,260 --> 00:16:18,637
You really expect me to
buy this load of baloney?

280
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,838
I think you've lost your touch, boy.

281
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:23,019
We found them, shouted Whole Horse.

282
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:26,200
Joseph, Jotaro, Polnareff, and Avdol.

283
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:27,968
Darn it, Whole Horse fumed.

284
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:30,977
They're a hop skippin' a jump
away from Master Dio's manor.

285
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:34,177
Those nosy buffoons will each
get a bullet between the eyes.

286
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:36,517
Whole Horse's mind was
full of violent thoughts.

287
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,482
You're gonna pay for my brother!

288
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:41,555
Mundata was beside himself with anger,

289
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:44,137
but despite the pair
wanting immediate payback,

290
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:47,808
Whole Horse couldn't use his
gun, the Emperor, in the market.

291
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,336
Now whole horse, Mondatta instructed,

292
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:55,776
stick your fingers all the way up
Polnareff's nose, and then we'll win!

293
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:58,537
They're out cold from
losing all that blood.

294
00:16:58,620 --> 00:16:59,877
Lucky you, whole horse.

295
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:02,784
This is your chance to
finish them off for good!

296
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,860
Like hell I'm gonna buy that!

297
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:07,440
This is your big premonition?

298
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:11,057
Sticking my callous fingers up
Polnareff's booger-infested nose?

299
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:12,617
The hell do you take me for?

300
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:14,220
Well, speak, Mondatta!

301
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:16,717
The part about killing
him sounds good to me.

302
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:17,657
but the rest of it?

303
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:20,257
You better not be planning
anything funny, boy.

304
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:21,640
I mean, come on.

305
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:24,817
Even if I was supposed to stick
my fingers at Polnareff's nose,

306
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:28,018
I'd have to somehow get
close enough to him to do it.

307
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:30,637
Instead of all that skullduggery?

308
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,117
I think we should go
with the direct approach.

309
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:33,957
and put a bullet in him with Emperor.

310
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:34,981
What do you say?

311
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:38,025
You're not gonna be able
to fire a bullet, yes.

312
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:42,280
Even though you tried firing your
stand, fate wouldn't let you, yes.

313
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:44,409
You have to trust me, yes.

314
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:45,877
I know from personal experience,

315
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:49,157
If you try to go against the comic,
you'll suffer the consequences.

316
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,357
It's fate, I tell you.

317
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:53,840
It's 100 % up to the whims
of fate. Yes. Hang on.

318
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:56,964
Your brother followed the
comic and nearly died.

319
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:00,375
My brother was trying to save himself,

320
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,417
but he foolishly disguised himself
as Jotaro without thinking.

321
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:04,330
Yes.

322
00:18:04,413 --> 00:18:06,877
If he had trusted what he read
and not disguised himself,

323
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:09,157
then the real Jotaro
would have been blown up.

324
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:10,070
Yes.

325
00:18:10,153 --> 00:18:12,620
The premonition itself was correct. Yes.

326
00:18:14,140 --> 00:18:15,280
Then what now?

327
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,220
Hm? Wait!

328
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:18,813
Where did Polnareff go?

329
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:20,180
Hey, kid!

330
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:21,792
Polnareff left the herd!

331
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:23,653
Find out where he went!

332
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,540
Shit! It can't be!

333
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,220
Don't you move!

334
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,824
Unless you'd like to be lanced.

335
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:33,550
But...

336
00:18:33,633 --> 00:18:34,960
how the hell did you...

337
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:46,357
Ombissile, what exactly did you think
you were trying to pull just now?

338
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:50,558
If you know what's good for you,
keep your hands where I can see them.

339
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:55,097
I thought I noticed someone stalking
us like a desperate, starving hyena.

340
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:58,537
And wouldn't you know, I was lucky
enough to stumble across our old friend,

341
00:18:58,620 --> 00:18:59,450
Whole Horse.

342
00:18:59,533 --> 00:19:01,397
It looks like you're
still trying to kill us,

343
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:04,037
which means you haven't
learned your lesson yet.

344
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:06,640
Say, thanks for all the fun back in India.

345
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:11,864
You're very lucky Avdol survived our run-in,
because if he hadn't, you, my friend,

346
00:19:12,060 --> 00:19:13,500
would already be dead.

347
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:16,700
You here alone, whole horse?

348
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:18,080
No way.

349
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:20,709
A coward like you
wouldn't come by himself.

350
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,520
I'm sure he's hiding out nearby, right?

351
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:25,580
Well, where's your partner?

352
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:26,930
Crap!

353
00:19:27,013 --> 00:19:29,577
On the upside, though, he
hasn't noticed Mondatta yet.

354
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:30,954
I still have a chance.

355
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,110
Shit!

356
00:19:36,193 --> 00:19:38,334
He's gonna see the book in his fingers!

357
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:41,257
On your own, you're not much
of a threat, whole horse,

358
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:44,877
but I'm well aware that you have a
special talent for picking allies.

359
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:47,417
If you've found someone
to work with like before,

360
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:49,557
that could make you a dangerous obstacle.

361
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,699
Tell me, where did your partner go?

362
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:54,391
Out with it, where's the other stand user?

363
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:56,170
Your fingers!

364
00:19:56,253 --> 00:19:57,827
Mondatta, hide your fingers!

365
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:00,960
If it gets wise to where
you are, it's all over!

366
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:03,040
You have to believe.

367
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:07,177
The reason you're in this situation
is because you tried using your gun.

368
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:08,920
Trust me, believe in fate.

369
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:13,300
If you believe in the power of fate,
our victory is guaranteed. Yes?

370
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:21,820
I saw a hand go into the box,
which means my hunt was right.

371
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:23,417
What's the word, Polnareff?

372
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:26,029
Did you find the guy
that was following us?

373
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:29,900
Oh no, it's Avdor, and his
head is straight for us.

374
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:32,180
Believe! Yes!

375
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:36,860
Put your faith in the book and stick
your fingers up Polarap's nose! Yes!

376
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:39,620
Are you serious? Damn it!

377
00:20:43,180 --> 00:20:44,660
I've got no choice!

378
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:46,040
Fine, I'll do it!

379
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:49,938
You, under the crate, show yourself!

380
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:52,077
Now, while he's looking the other way!

381
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:54,101
I know you're hiding under there!

382
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:59,197
What the hell?!

383
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:00,420
Hell yeah!

384
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:09,510
Woohoo!

385
00:21:09,593 --> 00:21:11,617
Everyone bled so much they all passed out!

386
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:12,917
Lucky you, Hoo Horse.

387
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,200
Now's your chance to finish them off!

388
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:18,817
So, what is this so-called
chance supposed to get here?

389
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:20,488
And what do I do till then?

390
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:23,440
Excuse me, Hoo Horse?

391
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:25,317
What the hell are you doing?

392
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:28,377
You're not the only one who wants
to know the answer to that question.

393
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:31,257
I haven't the foggiest
idea where to go from here.

394
00:21:31,340 --> 00:21:33,180
What am I supposed to do?

395
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:36,676
Hey, what's the matter, polder after?

396
00:21:37,380 --> 00:21:38,940
He's not answering back.

397
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:40,441
Something's off.

398
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:41,800
Shit, what now?

399
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:44,037
You threw on me like white on rice.

400
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:44,950
Damn it.

401
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:49,060
How the hell do I make the rest of
this stupid prediction come true?

402
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:50,520
This is crazy.

403
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:52,640
What am I supposed to do?

404
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:58,380
Do you believe it?

405
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:00,200
I believe it!

406
00:22:00,860 --> 00:22:03,180
Hell Horse! Boingo! Copy!

407
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:06,060
I'm a Hell Horse!

408
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:13,397
The card is Emperor.

409
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:15,957
He's 2nd player.

410
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:22,700
It's a guy who is flying,
but it's okay to be a boy.

411
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:27,840
I'm a boy-in-go-manga-man-guerun.

412
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:30,757
I'm a boy-in-go-in-go-man-guerun.

413
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:34,137
I'm a boy-in-go-in-go-man-guerun.

414
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:35,517
I'm a man-guerun

415
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,757
-go-in

416
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:42,817
-go-in.

417
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:44,517
We'll see you soon, too!

418
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:45,600
This is the case!

419
00:22:46,980 --> 00:22:48,277
We'll see you soon!

420
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:49,889
We won't believe you soon!

421
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:54,680
The word for the book is
true! It's a great thing!

422
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,518
It's a great thing!

423
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:58,820
The story in the past!

424
00:22:59,900 --> 00:23:02,260
We'll see you soon!

425
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:04,840
You're all right!

426
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:06,450
You're right!

427
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:07,810
You're right!

428
00:23:07,893 --> 00:23:08,723
We're first!

429
00:23:08,806 --> 00:23:09,636
The boss!

430
00:23:09,719 --> 00:23:10,549
We're so good!

431
00:23:10,632 --> 00:23:11,462
I'm sure!

432
00:23:11,545 --> 00:23:12,375
I can't believe it.

433
00:23:12,458 --> 00:23:13,288
Yes.

434
00:23:13,371 --> 00:23:14,201
Okay, I can't believe it.

435
00:23:14,284 --> 00:23:15,114
I'm your horse.

436
00:23:15,197 --> 00:23:16,180
Boingo. Combi.

437
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:20,780
The only thing I can't read
is that I can't read properly.
